{
 "esm": "1.3.0",
 "metadata": {
  "name": "cism_transport",
  "description": "Stage-2 implementation of the pointwise slice of the CISM thickness/tracer solve (stage 2 of the EqESM project; CISM = cismwrap_3_00_002 / cism_main_3.00_002 as built in CESM cesm3.0-alphabranch, reference run T1850Gg/f09_g17_gris20; CISM_LANE.md rows 6/7/14): the parts of glissade_thickness_tracer_solve that are not horizontal/vertical grid operations. (a) GladSmb - the cap qsmb-to-acab conversion and the glad-level zeroing (libglad/glad_main.F90:810-824, libglad/glad_timestep.F90:171-187): acab = qsmb*tstep_mbal*3600/rhoi [m/yr ice, with tstep_mbal = 8760 h = 1 yr in the reference run], then acab = 0 where thck <= 0 and acab < 0 (ice-free ablation) and where the cell is ice-free ocean (GLIDE_IS_OCEAN: topg < eus and no ice, glide_mask.inc:33-34). The further cap 'acab = -thck_temp' of glad_timestep.F90:233-235 is applied AFTER glide_set_acab and only adjusts the glad output variable, not the applied field - it is documented, not transcribed. (b) MassBalance - the surface/basal mass-balance application of add_surface_and_basal_mass_balance (libglissade/glissade_mass_balance.F90:819-1571) as a continuous rate law d(thck)/dt = acab - bmlt (m/yr ice; bmlt = bmlt_ground + bmlt_float) applied to the unclipped thickness state thck_raw with the physical thickness thck = max(0, thck_raw) - the Fortran's layer-by-layer removal clips the column at zero - the per-step melt_potential = max(0, -(thck + (acab-bmlt)*dt)) of fully melted columns (a per-step diagnostic in the Fortran, not a model state: it is zeroed at the top of every mass_balance_driver call, F90:1096; the esm form reproduces the per-step value when started at zero, which is how the tests pin it), the applied-rate bookkeeping acab_applied/bmlt_applied in their exact per-step forms, the tracer surface/bed handling: the layer-1 accumulation blend T1' = (H1*T1 + s*Tsurf)/(H1 + s) with H1 = sigma2*thck (new snow arrives at the current surface temperature temp(0), glissade_transport.F90:166), the layer-10 freeze-on blend T10' = (H10*T10 + b*Tbed)/(H10 + b) with H10 = (1 - sigma10)*thck (freeze-on arrives at the bed temperature temp(upn), F90:172-174), the column-mean temperature law Tbar' = (thck*Tbar + s*Tsurf + b*Tbed)/(thck + s + b) for accumulation/freeze-on and Tbar' = (thck*Tbar + s*T1)/(thck + s) for ablation (the Fortran removes the ablated ice from the top layers; the layer-free form removes it at the layer-1 temperature, exact while the ablation stays within layer 1, see README-cism-transport.md), the tracer zeroing of fully melted layers (tracer = 0, F90:1411-1413), the ice-age increment d(age)/dt = 1 where thck > 0 (libglissade/glissade.F90:1203-1213) with age_usrf = 0 and age_lsrf = age (the tracer surface/bed values of glissade_transport.F90:204-208), and the sigma layer thicknesses via the glide stretched-sigma template (cism_templates.esm cism_sigma, libglide/glide_setup.F90:303-308, 380-387). (c) SurfaceUpdate - the post-transport surface/bed elevation cleanup calc_lsrf_usrf (libglimmer/glimmer_utils.F90:344-378): lsrf = topg where grounded, lsrf = eus - (rhoi/rhoo)*thck where floating, usrf = lsrf + thck. The horizontal transport and the first-order vertical remap (libglissade/glissade_transport.F90) are grid operations that need the discretization machinery and live in the stage-3 assembly; the tests pin the SMB application, tracer surface/bed handling and cleanup against the cism_transport.csv dump (phase=entry before transport, phase=exit after SMB and cleanup), with the horizontal-advection residuals documented in README-cism-transport.md. The reference window has bmlt_ground = bmlt_float = 0 everywhere (cold base, no shelf melt) and no ice-age dump column, so the basal-melt/freeze-on branches and the age law are pinned from the source formulas."
  },
  "models": {
   "GladSmb": {
    "variables": {
     "qsmb": {
      "type": "parameter",
      "units": "kg/m^2/s",
      "default": 0.0,
      "description": "surface mass balance from the cap (glad_inputs%qsmb, kg m-2 s-1 = mm s-1; the cism_cap.csv import column, accumulated over the mass-balance window)"
     },
     "tstep_mbal": {
      "type": "parameter",
      "units": "h",
      "default": 8760.0,
      "description": "mass-balance accumulation window (params%tstep_mbal, hours; glad_main.F90:814-816). 8760 h = 1 yr in the reference run, so the conversion is numerically m/yr ice"
     },
     "rhoi": {
      "type": "parameter",
      "units": "kg/m^3",
      "default": 917.0,
      "description": "ice density (glimmer_physcon rhoi = 917 kg/m3)"
     },
     "windows_per_year": {
      "type": "parameter",
      "units": "1/yr",
      "default": 1.0,
      "description": "number of mass-balance accumulation windows per year = 8760 h / tstep_mbal; 1 for the reference run (tstep_mbal = 8760 h = 1 yr). Converts the per-window accumulation of the glad conversion into the per-year rate of the dump's acab column (glad_main.F90:810-824 accumulates over the window; the dump labels the result m/yr ice)"
     },
     "thck": {
      "type": "parameter",
      "units": "m",
      "default": 0.0,
      "description": "ice thickness at the time of the glad step (glide_geometry%thck, m; the pre-step thickness used by the glad-level zeroing)"
     },
     "topg": {
      "type": "parameter",
      "units": "m",
      "default": 0.0,
      "description": "bedrock topography elevation (glide_geometry%topg, m)"
     },
     "eus": {
      "type": "parameter",
      "units": "m",
      "default": 0.0,
      "description": "eustatic sea level (model%climate%eus, m; 0 in the reference run)"
     },
     "ocean": {
      "type": "unknown",
      "units": "1",
      "default": 0.0,
      "description": "GLIDE_IS_OCEAN: bed below sea level and no ice (glide_mask.inc:33-34; the OCEAN bit of the thkmask is set where topg < eus, glide_set_geometry)"
     },
     "acab_raw": {
      "type": "unknown",
      "units": "m/yr",
      "default": 0.0,
      "description": "unmasked surface mass balance = qsmb*tstep_mbal*3600/rhoi*windows_per_year (m/yr ice; glad_main.F90:810-824, where the rhow factor of the Fortran cancels: qsmb*3600*tstep_mbal is kg/m2 over the window, divided by rhoi gives m of ice per window, and windows_per_year = 1 turns it into the per-year rate of the dump column)"
     },
     "acab": {
      "type": "unknown",
      "units": "m/yr",
      "default": 0.0,
      "description": "the surface mass balance as applied to the ice sheet (m/yr ice; model%climate%acab after the glad-level zeroing of glad_timestep.F90:171-187 and the m/yr conversion of glide_set_acab)"
     }
    },
    "equations": [
     {
      "lhs": "ocean",
      "rhs": {
       "op": "ifelse",
       "args": [
        {
         "op": "and",
         "args": [
          {
           "op": "<=",
           "args": [
            "thck",
            {
             "op": "const",
             "args": [],
             "value": 0.0,
             "units": "m"
            }
           ]
          },
          {
           "op": "<",
           "args": [
            "topg",
            "eus"
           ]
          }
         ]
        },
        {
         "op": "const",
         "args": [],
         "value": 1.0,
         "units": "1"
        },
        {
         "op": "const",
         "args": [],
         "value": 0.0,
         "units": "1"
        }
       ]
      }
     },
     {
      "lhs": "acab_raw",
      "rhs": {
       "op": "/",
       "args": [
        {
         "op": "*",
         "args": [
          "qsmb",
          "tstep_mbal",
          {
           "op": "const",
           "args": [],
           "value": 3600.0,
           "units": "s/h"
          },
          "windows_per_year"
         ]
        },
        "rhoi"
       ]
      }
     },
     {
      "lhs": "acab",
      "rhs": {
       "op": "ifelse",
       "args": [
        {
         "op": "==",
         "args": [
          "ocean",
          {
           "op": "const",
           "args": [],
           "value": 1.0,
           "units": "1"
          }
         ]
        },
        {
         "op": "const",
         "args": [],
         "value": 0.0,
         "units": "m/yr"
        },
        {
         "op": "ifelse",
         "args": [
          {
           "op": "and",
           "args": [
            {
             "op": "<=",
             "args": [
              "thck",
              {
               "op": "const",
               "args": [],
               "value": 0.0,
               "units": "m"
              }
             ]
            },
            {
             "op": "<",
             "args": [
              "acab_raw",
              {
               "op": "const",
               "args": [],
               "value": 0.0,
               "units": "m/yr"
              }
             ]
            }
           ]
          },
          {
           "op": "const",
           "args": [],
           "value": 0.0,
           "units": "m/yr"
          },
          "acab_raw"
         ]
        }
       ]
      }
     }
    ],
    "tests": [
     {
      "id": "qsmb_to_acab_step1_cell2511",
      "description": "Dump pin, cism_cap.csv import row (cap_step 1, cell 25,11): qsmb = 4.05302216536369290e-06 kg/m2/s, tstep_mbal = 8760 h, rhoi = 917 kg/m3 give acab_raw = qsmb*8760*3600/917 = 0.13938506761931235 m/yr ice, identical to the cism_transport.csv entry acab of the same cell at step 1 (rel 0.0e+00 on all 64 traced cells, see README-cism-transport.md). thck = 1.30004894733428955 m > 0, so no zeroing fires and acab = acab_raw.",
      "time_span": {
       "start": 0.0,
       "end": 0.0
      },
      "parameter_overrides": {
       "qsmb": 4.05302216536369290e-06,
       "thck": 1.30004894733428955,
       "topg": 1082.0
      },
      "assertions": [
       {
        "variable": "acab_raw",
        "time": 0.0,
        "expected": 0.13938506761931235,
        "tolerance": {
         "rel": 1e-12
        }
       },
       {
        "variable": "acab",
        "time": 0.0,
        "expected": 0.13938506761931235,
        "tolerance": {
         "rel": 1e-12
        }
       },
       {
        "variable": "ocean",
        "time": 0.0,
        "expected": 0.0
       }
      ]
     },
     {
      "id": "qsmb_to_acab_cap2_cell2511",
      "description": "Dump pin, cism_cap.csv import row (cap_step 2, cell 25,11): qsmb = -1.69074734385490992e-05 kg/m2/s gives acab = -0.58145483354207683 m/yr ice, identical to the cism_transport.csv entry acab of the same cell at step 3 (the ablation year). thck = 1.4394647029325882 m > 0, so the ice-free zeroing does not fire.",
      "time_span": {
       "start": 0.0,
       "end": 0.0
      },
      "parameter_overrides": {
       "qsmb": -1.69074734385490992e-05,
       "thck": 1.4394647029325882,
       "topg": 1082.0
      },
      "assertions": [
       {
        "variable": "acab",
        "time": 0.0,
        "expected": -0.58145483354207683,
        "tolerance": {
         "rel": 1e-12
        }
       }
      ]
     },
     {
      "id": "qsmb_to_acab_step1_cell2611",
      "description": "Dump pin, cism_cap.csv import row (cap_step 1, cell 26,11): the largest traced accumulation qsmb = 6.05103156348133181e-05 kg/m2/s gives acab = 2.0809741699667099 m/yr ice, identical to the cism_transport.csv entry acab (step 1).",
      "time_span": {
       "start": 0.0,
       "end": 0.0
      },
      "parameter_overrides": {
       "qsmb": 6.05103156348133181e-05,
       "thck": 14.0,
       "topg": 1752.9000244140625
      },
      "assertions": [
       {
        "variable": "acab",
        "time": 0.0,
        "expected": 2.0809741699667099,
        "tolerance": {
         "rel": 1e-12
        }
       }
      ]
     },
     {
      "id": "zeroing_icefree_ablation_cell2811_step2",
      "description": "Dump pin of the glad-level ice-free zeroing (glad_timestep.F90:171-175): the cism_transport.csv entry row of cell 28,11 at step 2 has thck = 0 exactly (the step-1 SMB melted the 0.0199585 m column out) and the dump's acab column reads 0 - the raw cap value for cap_step 1 (qsmb = -2.05729925935643034e-05 kg/m2/s, i.e. acab_raw = -0.7075135162820545 m/yr ice) is zeroed because thck <= 0 and acab_raw < 0. The acab_raw assertion pins the raw value; the acab = 0 assertion pins the zeroing.",
      "time_span": {
       "start": 0.0,
       "end": 0.0
      },
      "parameter_overrides": {
       "qsmb": -2.05729925935643034e-05,
       "thck": 0.0,
       "topg": 921.1400146484375
      },
      "assertions": [
       {
        "variable": "acab_raw",
        "time": 0.0,
        "expected": -0.7075135162820545,
        "tolerance": {
         "rel": 1e-12
        }
       },
       {
        "variable": "acab",
        "time": 0.0,
        "expected": 0.0
       }
      ]
     },
     {
      "id": "thin_ice_no_zeroing_cell2811_step3",
      "description": "Dump pin of the zeroing branch boundary: the cism_transport.csv entry row of cell 28,11 at step 3 has thck = 1.6503583323323985e-05 m > 0 (thin ice advected in during step 2) and the dump's acab column reads -1.7674468845051972 m/yr ice - the raw cap_step-2 value (qsmb = -5.13936070868615494e-05 kg/m2/s), NOT zeroed: the glad-level condition thck <= 0 fails for any ice at all, however thin.",
      "time_span": {
       "start": 0.0,
       "end": 0.0
      },
      "parameter_overrides": {
       "qsmb": -5.13936070868615494e-05,
       "thck": 1.6503583323323985e-05,
       "topg": 921.1400146484375
      },
      "assertions": [
       {
        "variable": "acab",
        "time": 0.0,
        "expected": -1.7674468845051972,
        "tolerance": {
         "rel": 1e-12
        }
       }
      ]
     },
     {
      "id": "zeroing_ocean_synthetic",
      "description": "The ocean-cell zeroing branch, from the SOURCE FORMULA (glad_timestep.F90:177-178, GLIDE_IS_OCEAN = bed below sea level and no ice, glide_mask.inc:33-34): an ice-free cell below sea level (topg = -100 m < eus = 0, thck = 0) gets acab = 0 even for a positive qsmb - the ocean zeroing is independent of the sign of acab (no traced cell is ocean in the reference window; all 32 traced cells have topg >= 921 m).",
      "time_span": {
       "start": 0.0,
       "end": 0.0
      },
      "parameter_overrides": {
       "qsmb": 1.0e-04,
       "thck": 0.0,
       "topg": -100.0
      },
      "assertions": [
       {
        "variable": "ocean",
        "time": 0.0,
        "expected": 1.0
       },
       {
        "variable": "acab",
        "time": 0.0,
        "expected": 0.0
       }
      ]
     }
    ]
   },
   "MassBalance": {
    "expression_template_imports": [
     {
      "ref": "./cism_templates.esm"
     }
    ],
    "variables": {
     "acab": {
      "type": "parameter",
      "units": "m/yr",
      "default": 0.0,
      "description": "surface mass balance (m/yr ice), as zeroed by GladSmb (model%climate%acab, m/s in the Fortran; glad_timestep.F90:171-187)"
     },
     "bmlt": {
      "type": "parameter",
      "units": "m/yr",
      "default": 0.0,
      "description": "basal melt rate bmlt_ground + bmlt_float (m/yr ice; positive melting, negative freeze-on; model%basal_melt%bmlt, glissade_apply_smb F90:842-850). 0 everywhere in the reference window (cold base, no shelf melt), so the bmlt branches are pinned from the source formula"
     },
     "topg": {
      "type": "parameter",
      "units": "m",
      "default": 0.0,
      "description": "bedrock topography elevation (m), for the ocean mask"
     },
     "eus": {
      "type": "parameter",
      "units": "m",
      "default": 0.0,
      "description": "eustatic sea level (m; 0 in the reference run)"
     },
     "dt": {
      "type": "parameter",
      "units": "yr",
      "default": 0.5,
      "description": "dynamics time step (model%numerics%dt, yr; 0.5 yr in the reference run: two dynamics steps per cap year)"
     },
     "x_sigma2": {
      "type": "parameter",
      "units": "1",
      "default": 0.1,
      "description": "normalized level of the layer-1 interface: x = (up-1)/(upn-1) = 1/10 for upn = 11 (glide_setup.F90:303-308)"
     },
     "x_sigma10": {
      "type": "parameter",
      "units": "1",
      "default": 0.9,
      "description": "normalized level of the layer-10 interface: x = 9/10 for upn = 11"
     },
     "n_sigma": {
      "type": "parameter",
      "units": "1",
      "default": 2.0,
      "description": "SIGMA_COMPUTE_GLIDE stretch exponent n = 2 (glide_setup.F90:303-308)"
     },
     "T1": {
      "type": "parameter",
      "units": "degC",
      "default": 0.0,
      "description": "pre-step layer-1 temperature (model%temper%temp(1,:,:), degC)"
     },
     "Tbar": {
      "type": "parameter",
      "units": "degC",
      "default": 0.0,
      "description": "pre-step column-mean temperature over layers 1..10 (the layer-free representation of the temperature tracer column)"
     },
     "Tsurf": {
      "type": "parameter",
      "units": "degC",
      "default": 0.0,
      "description": "upper-surface temperature temp(0), the temperature of new accumulation (tracers_usrf of the temperature tracer, glissade_transport.F90:166)"
     },
     "Tbed": {
      "type": "parameter",
      "units": "degC",
      "default": 0.0,
      "description": "lower-surface temperature temp(upn), the temperature of basal freeze-on (tracers_lsrf, glissade_transport.F90:172-174)"
     },
     "T10": {
      "type": "parameter",
      "units": "degC",
      "default": 0.0,
      "description": "pre-step layer-10 temperature (model%temper%temp(10,:,:), degC)"
     },
     "sigma2": {
      "type": "unknown",
      "units": "1",
      "default": 0.0,
      "description": "glide sigma level 2 = glide_calc_sigma(0.1, 2) = 0.23140495867768607 (glide_setup.F90:380-387); the layer-1 thickness fraction"
     },
     "sigma10": {
      "type": "unknown",
      "units": "1",
      "default": 0.0,
      "description": "glide sigma level 10 = glide_calc_sigma(0.9, 2) = 0.96398891966759004; the layer-10 thickness fraction is 1 - sigma10"
     },
     "ocean_mask": {
      "type": "unknown",
      "units": "1",
      "default": 0.0,
      "description": "ocean mask of the mass-balance driver: 1 where topg < eus and thck <= thklim = 0, else 0 (glissade_get_masks, glissade_masks.F90:70-96; the SMB and BMB are not applied to ocean cells, glissade_mass_balance.F90:1333-1341)"
     },
     "net": {
      "type": "unknown",
      "units": "m/yr",
      "default": 0.0,
      "description": "unmasked net mass balance acab - bmlt (m/yr ice)"
     },
     "net_applied": {
      "type": "unknown",
      "units": "m/yr",
      "default": 0.0,
      "description": "net mass balance actually applied: 0 in ocean cells, else net (the Fortran's ocean_mask guard, F90:1333-1341, and the effective_areafrac = 0 of ocean cells, F90:893-901)"
     },
     "thck_raw": {
      "type": "unknown",
      "units": "m",
      "default": 0.0,
      "description": "unclipped ice thickness (m). The Fortran removes the ablation layer by layer and clips the column at zero (F90:1398-1419); the esm model integrates the unclipped thickness and clamps the output, which is exact at step boundaries for the constant-net steps of the dump"
     },
     "thck": {
      "type": "unknown",
      "units": "m",
      "default": 0.0,
      "description": "physical ice thickness (m) = max(0, thck_raw), the clipped column thickness of the Fortran (glide_geometry%thck after the SMB application)"
     },
     "melt_potential": {
      "type": "unknown",
      "units": "m",
      "default": 0.0,
      "description": "total thickness (m) of additional ice that could have been melted by the available acab/bmlt in columns that melted out completely: max(0, -thck_raw) (the Fortran's per-step melt_potential accumulator of F90:1418-1422/1452-1457, zeroed at the top of every mass_balance_driver call - it is a per-step diagnostic, not a model state; the esm form reproduces the per-step value for a step starting from an ice-covered state, which is what the tests pin; not a dump column)"
     },
     "H_pre": {
      "type": "unknown",
      "units": "m",
      "default": 0.0,
      "description": "pre-step ice thickness (m): thck_raw - net_applied*dt is the thickness at the start of the step for constant net, the thickness the Fortran's layer loops start from (F90:1330-1332, thck_layer = thck*(sigma(k+1)-sigma(k)))"
     },
     "s": {
      "type": "unknown",
      "units": "m",
      "default": 0.0,
      "description": "signed surface thickness change per step (m): acab*dt; positive accumulation, negative ablation"
     },
     "b": {
      "type": "unknown",
      "units": "m",
      "default": 0.0,
      "description": "freeze-on thickness per step (m): -bmlt*dt for bmlt < 0, else 0 (bed_accum, F90:1455-1456)"
     },
     "H1": {
      "type": "unknown",
      "units": "m",
      "default": 0.0,
      "description": "pre-step layer-1 thickness = sigma2*H_pre (thck_layer(:,:,1), F90:1330-1332)"
     },
     "H10": {
      "type": "unknown",
      "units": "m",
      "default": 0.0,
      "description": "pre-step layer-10 thickness = (1 - sigma10)*H_pre"
     },
     "acab_applied": {
      "type": "unknown",
      "units": "m/yr",
      "default": 0.0,
      "description": "surface mass balance actually applied (m/yr ice; model%climate%acab_applied, m/s in the Fortran): the full acab while the column survives, -H_pre/dt when the ablation removes the whole column (F90:1385-1422; the Fortran accumulates the applied amount in m per step and converts back to m/s at F90:1567). Not a dump column (the dump carries the input acab, not the applied value) - pinned from the source formula at the full-melt pins"
     },
     "bmlt_applied": {
      "type": "unknown",
      "units": "m/yr",
      "default": 0.0,
      "description": "basal melt rate actually applied (m/yr ice; model%basal_melt%bmlt_applied): the full bmlt for freeze-on and for basal melt while the column survives, the remaining column thickness per step when the melt removes it all (F90:1437-1457). Not a dump column; pinned from the source formula at the full-melt pins (bmlt = 0 in the reference window, so bmlt_applied = 0 there)"
     },
     "T1_out": {
      "type": "unknown",
      "units": "degC",
      "default": 0.0,
      "description": "layer-1 temperature after the SMB application: the accumulation blend (H1*T1 + s*Tsurf)/(H1 + s) of F90:1380-1386 (new ice arrives at the surface temperature), unchanged by ablation while the ablation stays within layer 1 (F90:1398-1413 removes ice without changing the tracer; the layer-free model keeps T1 once the ablated depth exceeds H1 - the layer-2 identity is lost, a documented approximation), and 0 in fully melted columns (the tracer = 0 of F90:1411-1413; the dump's exit temp_001 of the melted cells reads 0 exactly)"
     },
     "Tbar_out": {
      "type": "unknown",
      "units": "degC",
      "default": 0.0,
      "description": "column-mean temperature after the SMB application: (H_pre*Tbar + s*Tsurf + b*Tbed)/(H_pre + s + b) for accumulation/freeze-on and (H_pre*Tbar + s*T1)/(H_pre + s) for ablation (mass x tracer conservation of the Fortran's layer updates; the ablation removes the top layers, approximated at the layer-1 temperature - exact while the ablated depth stays within layer 1, see README-cism-transport.md), 0 in fully melted columns"
     },
     "T10_out": {
      "type": "unknown",
      "units": "degC",
      "default": 0.0,
      "description": "layer-10 temperature after the SMB application: the freeze-on blend (H10*T10 + b*Tbed)/(H10 + b) of F90:1458-1465 (freeze-on arrives at the bed temperature), unchanged otherwise, 0 in fully melted columns"
     },
     "age": {
      "type": "unknown",
      "units": "yr",
      "default": 0.0,
      "description": "ice age (yr; model%geometry%ice_age, seconds internally, converted to years on output). Incremented d(age)/dt = 1 where thck > 0 (glissade.F90:1203-1213). The Fortran additionally RESETS the age to 0 on ice-free cells (F90:1209-1213); the ODE form only stops the increment - the reset is unobservable in the reference window (no traced cell refreezes) and is a documented difference for the stage-3 assembly. Not a dump column"
     },
     "age_usrf": {
      "type": "unknown",
      "units": "yr",
      "default": 0.0,
      "description": "ice age of new surface accumulation = 0 (tracers_usrf of the age tracer, glissade_transport.F90:204-206)"
     },
     "age_lsrf": {
      "type": "unknown",
      "units": "yr",
      "default": 0.0,
      "description": "ice age of basal freeze-on = the bottom-layer age (tracers_lsrf, glissade_transport.F90:207-208); the layer-free model's bottom-layer age is the age state"
     }
    },
